COLOUR VISION — 3 pair(s) distinct to you that lose their distinction for a red-green colour vision deficiency (~8% of men, ~0.5% of women):
  deuteranopia  #116B8A vs #7044A0  ->  #5B5B8B vs #5454A0   (23% of the separation left)
  protanopia    #116B8A vs #4E626C  ->  #65658A vs #60606C   (48% of the separation left)
  deuteranopia  #116B8A vs #4E626C  ->  #5B5B8B vs #5D5D6C   (48% of the separation left)
  This matters only where the two carry MEANING — a series, a status, a legend. Where they do, separate them by LIGHTNESS or by shape/label as well as hue, or take the categorical set from deckkit.OKABE_ITO, which is built for this.

